      "content": "exactly. so if it actually \"overrides slower, critical thinking\" like you said, then we're talking about something much more predatory than just marketing. it's almost like they've engineered a cognitive loophole to exploit people's vulnerabilities. if the design is mathematically tuned to bypass our ability to make rational choices, doesn't that move it from \"persuasion\" into actual psychological manipulation? like, a form of neuro-targeted coercion? it makes me wonder how many other brands are using these specific geometric patterns to essentially hack our decision-making processes.",
